<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 1174) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Reports, redesigned:</b> the notes report and the review activity report now use Asobi&#8217;s own design, like the manual: numbered entries, the notes in a readable serif with a byline each, replies under their notes, and nothing split across a page.</li>
<li><b>Spell check in comments:</b> notes and replies get the Mac&#8217;s red underline, with right-click suggestions. Autocorrect is there too if you want it: Settings ▸ Notes or Edit ▸ Spelling in Comments.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1170) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Timeline markers:</b> notes show as a blue line, markup as an amber triangle on the top edge, like a mark in an edit application. A frame with both shows both.</li>
<li><b>Replies:</b> a Send button appears beside a reply as you type (Return still sends).</li>
<li><b>Note report:</b> replies print under their notes, the comment text is larger, and small markup is shown magnified with the whole frame as an inset that stays clear of the marks.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1165) <span class="when">Oct 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Menus during playback:</b> the menu bar&#8217;s menus and submenus stay put and take clicks while a clip plays.</li>
<li><b>Aspect ratio bars in exports:</b> the QuickTime export&#8217;s Burn in options can add black bars outside the tightest guide on screen, with or without the frame lines and labels.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1162) <span class="when">Oct 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Steadier while playing:</b> menus no longer flicker or miss clicks during playback, and the toolbar keeps its width.</li>
<li><b>Volume:</b> the Sound button opens a vertical volume slider with mute at the bottom (M still mutes).</li>
<li><b>Aspect guides:</b> add your own ratio with Custom Ratio… (2.2, 2.20:1, 4:5 or 1920x800) — web reviewers see it too. The mask is now three simple choices: No Mask, Dim Outside, Hard Mask.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1157) <span class="when">Oct 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Frame lines:</b> View ▸ Aspect Guides now has Lines (on or off) and Mask (None, Dim Outside, Hard Mask) — so a mask can show on its own. Something always shows while guides are on.</li>
<li><b>Kitsu:</b> the status choices load as soon as you sign in.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1153) <span class="when">Oct 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Frame lines:</b> View ▸ Aspect Guides ▸ Style draws them as lines, dims everything outside the frame, or masks it to black. Web reviewers now see your frame lines too, and can pick their own style.</li>
<li><b>Volume:</b> the arrow beside the Sound button opens a volume slider.</li>
<li><b>Find Originals</b> is smarter: it uses each Kitsu clip&#8217;s comment path whatever folder you point it at, matches Kitsu&#8217;s own clip names, and searches inside any folder you choose. Source Links remembers its folder.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1144) <span class="when">Oct 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Find Originals:</b> in Review ▸ Set Source Links…, one button finds each clip&#8217;s original on the projects drive: the path in its Kitsu comment, or the render for its shot and version (the frames before a movie). Each clip says how it was found.</li>
<li>A copy that isn&#8217;t activated can still join reviews hosted by Autonomy.</li>
<li>What&#8217;s New shows ▸, … and other characters correctly.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1139) <span class="when">Oct 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Activation:</b> Asobi ▸ Activate Asobi… walks you through activating this Mac and confirms it. Afterwards Asobi ▸ Asobi Activation… shows who it is activated for and when it ends, with Request an Extension… if it has an end date. The About window shows it too.</li>
<li>The link in the activation email now works in every mail app, Gmail included.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
